# Low Water, the second daylight page between Acts 2 and 3: "Before the Wind". Director's file.
# Plan: design/ACT3-PLAN.md section 5. Playable, in colour, no checks. Two calls of four before
# the light goes at 15:30, one small act of the player's in each; Wenna's call asks (the keeper
# plant, editor A11); Fisk's call pays nothing.

# ---- new ids
@fact day2.wenna
@fact day2.pip
@fact day2.boats
@fact day2.fisk
@fact day2.sleep
@var day2_calls
default: 0

@place day2_room
name: The room above the Brine, by day
zone: brine
district: brine
footing: wood
shelter: yes
light: 0.8
sodium: 0
dark-light: 0.8

@place day2_quay
name: Lamp Quay, before the wind
zone: quay
district: quay
footing: stone
light: 0.85
sodium: 0
dark-light: 0.85

@place day2_mole
name: The mole, before the wind
zone: mole
district: mole
footing: stone
light: 0.85
sodium: 0
dark-light: 0.85

@place day2_tube
name: The tube terminus, by day
zone: weigh
district: weigh
footing: wood
shelter: yes
light: 0.6
sodium: 0
dark-light: 0.6

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- waking
@node day2.start
place: day2_room
cost: 0
nar: One in the afternoon. The light through the planking is yellow and moves, because the clouds are moving, fast, all one way.
nar: The coat on its peg has two tide marks at the hem now, one above the other.
voice: salt: Something is coming up the coast. The knees knew before the Glass did. {dc: 3}
inst: THE GLASS: Nine hundred and sixty-two, darling, and the bottom's not in sight. Tonight the wind will want everything that isn't nailed down, and some things that are.
go: day2.quay

@node day2.quay
place: day2_quay
cost: 2
nar: Gullet in colour for the last time this week, and busy. Shutters going up over the oxblood and the mustard. Sabine and Teague are filling sacks with sand from a cart. Somebody on a ladder is roping the Brine's sign to the Brine.
nar: Out on the mole, small and dark against a sky the colour of a slate, a woman in an oxblood coat stands looking at the lamp.
go: day2.hub

@node day2.hub
hub: yes
place: day2_quay
alt: day2.dusk ? var.day2_calls >= 2 | clock >= 15:30
opt: "Walk out along the mole to Wenna." -> day2.wenna.go ? !has(day2.wenna) +10
opt: "Go to the tube, where Pip will be." -> day2.pip.go ? !has(day2.pip) +5
opt: "Go down to the boats, where they are making fast." -> day2.boats.go ? !has(day2.boats) +5
opt: "Go into the Brine, where the engineer is packing." -> day2.fisk.go ? !has(day2.fisk) +3
opt: "Go back up and sleep until the wind." -> day2.sleep.go

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Wenna asks (the keeper plant)
@node day2.wenna.go
place: day2_mole
cost: 15
do: set(day2.wenna); day2_calls += 1
nar: The spray is already coming over the rail in single sheets, a long time apart.
line: WENNA: She'll want a hand at the panel all night. Every time the board trips, and it will trip.
line: WENNA: My knees'll do the stairs once. Not twice. Not three times.
nar: She does not look at the assessor. She looks at the lamp.
opt: "Say you'll sit with her, if it comes to that." -> day2.wenna.yes
opt: "Say nothing, and look at the lamp too." -> day2.wenna.look

@node day2.wenna.yes
cost: 3
do: set(wenna.asked); set(said.day2_mother)
line: LAMB: If it comes to that.
line: WENNA: It'll come to that.
nar: She puts something in the assessor's hand without looking: a brass key on a string, warm from her neck.
go: day2.hub

@node day2.wenna.look
cost: 5
nar: They look at the lamp together until a sheet of spray reaches them both. Neither steps back.
line: WENNA: You'd do. If you had to.
do: set(wenna.asked)
go: day2.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Pip
@node day2.pip.go
place: day2_tube
cost: 10
do: set(day2.pip); day2_calls += 1
nar: Pip is on her crate by the brass mouth with the afternoon canister in her lap, unopened.
line: PIP: Can a person keep a promise for somebody that's gone? For a company that's gone, even?
nar: She turns the canister over. The cap is dented from years of being dropped onto the same hook.
opt: "Ask her who she means." -> day2.pip.who
opt: "Tell her a promise kept is a promise kept, whoever it was made to." -> day2.pip.answer

@node day2.pip.who
cost: 3
line: PIP: Nobody. Somebody I know. Forget I said.
nar: She hangs the canister on its hook without reading it, which, she told the assessor on the first night, is the shilling.
go: day2.hub

@node day2.pip.answer
cost: 3
do: set(said.day2_promise)
line: LAMB: A promise kept is kept. Whoever it was made to.
line: PIP: That's what she says.
nar: Pip hears what she has said a moment after she has said it, and goes red to the ears, in daylight, where everyone can see.
go: day2.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the boats
@node day2.boats.go
place: day2_quay
cost: 10
do: set(day2.boats); day2_calls += 1
alt: day2.boats.lugg ? has(merrow.cells) & !has(appt.joined)
nar: At the mole steps Merrow is doubling his lines, and then doubling the doubles. His boat rides low and clean.
line: MERROW: Eye comes over about a quarter past twelve. Forty minutes, if the Glass is honest. Forty minutes and you could row to the Old Light and back and have time to look.
nar: He holds out the end of a line.
opt: "Take it, and make it fast to the ring." -> day2.boats.rope
opt: "Leave the line to him." -> day2.hub

@node day2.boats.rope
cost: 5
nar: The assessor makes the line fast. Merrow undoes the knot without comment and makes it again, the way it is made.
line: MERROW: Boat's here at midnight. Whoever wants it.
do: rep(lowco, 1)
go: day2.hub

@node day2.boats.lugg
place: day2_quay
nar: Lugg is making the Company's boats fast alone. He works bent and careful, not looking up.
line: LUGG: Eye comes over at a quarter past twelve. Tub would go. Tub always goes.
opt: "Hold the bow while he ties it." -> day2.boats.hold
opt: "Leave him to it." -> day2.hub

@node day2.boats.hold
cost: 5
nar: The assessor holds the bow. Lugg ties it, and the next one, and then stands with his hand on the gunwale as if it were somebody's shoulder.
line: LUGG: Boat's here at midnight.
do: rep(lowco, 1)
go: day2.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Fisk (pays nothing)
@node day2.fisk.go
place: brine
cost: 10
do: set(day2.fisk); day2_calls += 1
nar: The engineer has his specifications spread on the Brine's table to dry. He is packing them into the satchel in an order that matters to him.
line: FISK: The coast road will be closed by four. I shall be stuck, assessor. I find I don't mind.
opt: "Help him put the pages in order." -> day2.fisk.help
opt: "Leave him to his satchel." -> day2.hub

@node day2.fisk.help
cost: 5
nar: The assessor hands him the pages by number. He takes each one as if it might be the last. Then one is.
line: FISK: Thank you. I am sorry about the adjectives.
go: day2.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sleep, dusk
@node day2.sleep.go
place: day2_room
cost: 0
do: set(day2.sleep); meter(wear, -10)
nar: The assessor lies down in the moving yellow light and listens to the town nail itself shut.
go: day2.dusk

@node day2.dusk
place: day2_quay
cost: 0
nar: At half past three the light goes the colour of a bruise, and then the colour of nothing, and the wind arrives at the end of the mole like a person who has run all the way.
go: quay3.start
